# Normalise line endings so the repository is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# text=auto lets Git detect text files and store them with LF in the repository.
# eol=lf pins the working copy to LF as well, overriding core.autocrlf (which is
# set to `true` system-wide on the Windows machine this was authored on).
#
# Without this, a fresh clone on Windows gets CRLF working copies while the
# repository holds LF, so the next `git add` renormalises and emits confusing
# whole-file diffs that contain no actual change. Pinning it here keeps diffs
# meaningful for anyone who clones the project or runs it in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf
